ine.com/markets/sensex-nifty-edge-down-on-profit-taking-inflation-worries/article71698030.ece", "status": "ok", "excerpt": "The Nifty declined 155.05 points or 0.61 per cent to 25,144.30, the Sensex slipped 318.56 points (0.39 per cent) to 81,592.45 and Bank Nifty fell 484.40 points (0.79 per cent) to 61,034.10\n\nBenchmark indices declined on Friday, but sustained the weekly gains, despite heavy buying by foreign institutional investors. Investors turned cautious due to inflationary pressures and renewed geopolitical tension and preferred to book profits on the recent bounce-back.\n\nOctober retail inflation climbed to 6.09 per cent, breaching the RBI\u2019s upper tolerance threshold of 6 per cent.\n\nHariselvan Radhakrishnan, Founder & CEO of HST Wealth, said Indian equities ended lower as rising domestic inflation and re", "citation": "Sensex, Nifty edge down on profit taking, inflation worries \u2014 BusinessLine Mkts, 2026-11-13. https://www.thehindubusinessline.com/markets/sensex-nifty-edge-down-on-profit-taking-inflation-worries/article71698030.ece"}, {"title": "Pulse of the Street: Dalal Street\u2019s winning streak faces an inflation test", "feed": "Mint Markets", "ts": "2026-11-13T13:53:34+00:00", "url": "https://www.livemint.com/market/stock-market-news/pulse-of-the-street-dalal-street-s-winning-streak-faces-an-inflation-test-11794572591011.html", "status": "ok", "excerpt": "This is a Mint Premium article gifted to you.Subscribe to enjoy similar stories.\n\nMUMBAI: Indian equities extended their winning streak to a third consecutive week, supported by stronger corporate earnings and sustained foreign buying. But the rally lost momentum, with rising inflation and continued domestic institutional selling raising questions about its durability.\n\nThe Nifty fell 0.6% on Friday to close at 25,144.30, while the Sensex declined 0.4% to 81,592.44. For the week, however, the indices gained 0.45% and 0.69%, respectively, following a nearly 9% surge in the previous week.\n\nImproving earnings offered support, with capital goods, financial services and realty stocks leading sect", "citation": "Pulse of the Street: Dalal Street\u2019s winning streak faces an inflation test \u2014 Mint Markets, 2026-11-13. https://www.livemint.com/market/stock-market-news/pulse-of-the-street-dalal-street-s-winning-streak-faces-an-inflation-test-11794572591011.html"}, {"title": "Diwali gains often last. Will this year\u2019s Sensex rally hold?", "feed": "Mint Markets", "ts": "2026-11-13T11:12:33+00:00", "url": "https://www.livemint.com/market/stock-market-news/diwali-gains-this-year-sensex-rally-muhurat-11794459314013.html", "status": "ok", "excerpt": "This is a Mint Premium article gifted to you.Subscribe to enjoy similar stories.\n\nThe festivities are over, but Dalal Street has held on to its cheer. The BSE Sensex gained 0.73% in the week after Muhurat trading on 8 November, adding to its strongest pre-Diwali weekly rally in three decades.\n\nThe 8.78% surge before Muhurat was the biggest, according to a Mint analysis of Bloomberg data from 1997 to 2026, well above the previous high of 5.4% in 2002. After such a sharp rise, the question is how much further the market can go.\n\nHistory offers some pointers. The Sensex rose in the week after Muhurat in 19 of the 29 years through 2025, or almost two-thirds of the time. But gains before the fest", "citation": "Diwali gains often last. Will this year\u2019s Sensex rally hold? \u2014 Mint Markets, 2026-11-13. https://www.livemint.com/market/stock-market-news/diwali-gains-this-year-sensex-rally-muhurat-11794459314013.html"}], "primary_sources": [{"series": "dyn_bajfinance_ns", "name": "Yahoo \u00b7 BAJFINANCE.NS", "url": "https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/BAJFINANCE.NS"}, {"series": "nifty_midcap_100", "name": "Yahoo \u00b7 NIFTY_MIDCAP_100.NS", "url": "https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/NIFTY_MIDCAP_100.NS"}, {"series": "nifty_50", "name": "Yahoo \u00b7 ^NSEI", "url": "https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/%5